WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.346 --> 00:00:02.921
Jesus lost followers over one sentence.

2
00:00:02.921 --> 00:00:06.486
In John chapter six he says, "my flesh is food indeed,

3
00:00:06.486 --> 00:00:10.446
and my blood is drink indeed." The crowd hears it literally,

4
00:00:10.446 --> 00:00:12.031
and they argue about it.

5
00:00:12.031 --> 00:00:15.463
If he meant a symbol, this was the moment to say so.

6
00:00:15.463 --> 00:00:16.850
He doesn't soften it.

7
00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.500
He says it more strongly:

8
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:22.659
unless you eat the flesh of the Son of Man and drink his blood,

9
00:00:22.659 --> 00:00:24.243
you have no life in you.

10
00:00:24.243 --> 00:00:28.138
And verse sixty-six says many of his disciples walked away.

11
00:00:28.588 --> 00:00:37.434
About twenty-five years later Saint Paul writes that whoever eats the bread unworthily will answer for the body and blood of the Lord.

12
00:00:37.434 --> 00:00:40.140
You can't sin against a picture that way.

13
00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:44.683
Then around the year one hundred and ten, Ignatius of Antioch,

14
00:00:44.683 --> 00:00:48.116
who learned the faith from the apostles' generation,

15
00:00:48.116 --> 00:00:57.160
warns about people who stay away from the Eucharist "because they confess not the Eucharist to be the flesh of our Saviour Jesus Christ."

16
00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:00.976
That's what the Church still teaches: Christ truly,

17
00:01:00.976 --> 00:01:03.155
really and substantially present.

18
00:01:03.155 --> 00:01:04.013
Not a symbol.

19
00:01:04.013 --> 00:01:04.277
Him.
